From ea76f21ca945197daf63f333f7ade61adae4ce0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:31:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): avoid unchanged containment trigger DDL on feed
 pages [daveey]

Why: every prepare_apply on a containment-enabled replica unconditionally
recreated eight triggers. Each page advanced schema_version by sixteen even
when only heartbeat/cursor bookkeeping changed. The links activity key includes
that cookie, so transport-only pages defeated the new unchanged-board skip.
The earlier links tests bypassed apply_remote_changes and missed this churn.

Generate the wanted trigger SQL, compare stored definitions, and replace only
missing/different triggers under the existing atomic writer transaction. When
definitions and marker observations are settled, register connection functions
but skip the writer transaction and INSERT backfill. Recheck after acquiring
the writer. Observation-trigger definitions also receive repair checks.

Preserve recovery of deleted marker observations: exact trigger coverage alone
is insufficient before a later task page clears its marker. A read-only anti-
join still scans task markers; this change does NOT claim to remove that scan
or meet the whole-family live CPU target. No TTL, active-stream, or pending-
terminal semantics change. Keep the failed-upgrade test with a real schema
upgrade precondition rather than requiring writes on an unchanged install.

Proof:
- Parent guard identical to 204e60d772: initial regression file 8 behavioral
  failures, including schema +16 and real heartbeat feed links-key change.
- Canonical 32 containment/links files: 527 passed, zero failed.
- Seven exact-anchor mutants killed: omitted fast return, writer recheck,
  selective DDL, SQL comparison, observation recovery, episode match, table guard.
- Full scripts/check --base origin/main passed.
- Real apply heartbeat pages preserve _links_inputs and skip reconcile/backfill;
  missing observations still survive a later marker-clear page as a hold.

Follow-up acceptance on owner t_09269f57c7cf61e6: independent exact-head review
and required CI, canonical ship, natural Mac deployment, then read-only idle
snapshot family <0.5% of a core at uptime >=3000s. No live measurement claimed.
